# Dev Notes 40 — Capability Router Namespace Cleanup v1

**Date:** 2026-06-15  
**Branch:** `capability-router-namespace-cleanup-v1`  
**Status:** Staged candidate; syntax-checked, contract-smoke-tested, helper-checked, and artifact-guarded in sandbox. Not yet repo-verified on GitHub.

---

## 1. Purpose

This branch performs a narrow namespace cleanup for the contract-only Capability Router helpers.

The router implementation modules move out of:

```text
runtime/bus/
```

and into:

```text
runtime/router/
```

The old `runtime/bus/` router paths remain as compatibility barrels so existing import paths do not hard-break.

---

## 2. Scope

In scope:

```text
move capability router implementation files to runtime/router/
keep runtime/bus router files as re-export-only compatibility barrels
update direct router imports in service/backend/router smoke tests
update service-plan import paths to the router namespace
update current docs for the new runtime/router namespace
add guard checks that router implementation lives under runtime/router/
add guard checks that runtime/bus router files are re-export-only barrels
```

Out of scope:

```text
executor contract
executeAction()
runtime.mjs public API changes
prompt() routing through Capability Bus
service execution
backend execution
nativeWorkerBackend implementation
workerBridge changes
llama_worker changes
lifecycle/request/stream/config changes
scheduler changes
configOverride expansion
model path/model identity changes
tool execution
memory/retrieval execution
Cognitive Graph Runtime implementation
service namespace migration
optimization work
unrelated cleanup
```

