## 5. Implementation summary

The implementation modules now live under:

```text
runtime/router/capabilityRouterCommon.mjs
runtime/router/capabilityRouteDefinition.mjs
runtime/router/capabilityRouterRegistry.mjs
runtime/router/capabilityRoutePlan.mjs
runtime/router/capabilityRouterContract.mjs
```

Router modules now import shared bus contract primitives from `runtime/bus/` where needed:

```text
contractValidation.mjs
actionEnvelope.mjs
capabilityBusContract.mjs
capabilityDefinition.mjs
capabilityTaxonomy.mjs
```

The old router paths under `runtime/bus/` are compatibility barrels only:

```js
export * from "../router/<same-file>.mjs";
```

`runtime/bus/capabilityServicePlan.mjs` imports router validation helpers directly from `runtime/router/` so the service-plan implementation depends on the router namespace instead of the bus compatibility path.

---

## 6. Guard additions

`tests/smokeTestCapabilityRouterContract.mjs` now checks:

```text
runtime/router/ contains the router implementation files
runtime/bus/ router files are re-export-only compatibility barrels
runtime/router/ router implementation files avoid runtime/worker execution imports
```

This is intentionally guard-style cleanup, not behavior expansion.

---

## 7. Architecture boundaries preserved

Preserved boundaries:

```text
queue-based concurrency
worker remains model/native execution boundary
parent runtime owns request lifecycle
parent-side stream shaping
config remains primary tuning surface
careful init/reset/shutdown behavior
prompt/output semantics unchanged
model identity/path guardrails unchanged
worker protocol shape unchanged
```

No runtime, worker, lifecycle, request, stream, config, scheduler, public API, backend execution, or service execution behavior was changed.

