## 11. Caveats / known risks

### Finding
The old `runtime/bus/` router files remain as compatibility barrels.

### Affected surface
Any current or future imports from the old router path.

### Why it matters
A hard move would break older path imports and create unnecessary branch friction before the executor contract branch.

### Smallest safe correction
Keep the compatibility barrels for this branch. Consider removing them only in a later explicitly approved breaking cleanup branch.

### What still needs verification
After upload, direct GitHub source inspection should confirm the moved implementation files and re-export-only compatibility barrels.

---

## 12. Recommended next step

After this cleanup branch is uploaded, tested locally by Michael, and repo-verified, proceed to:

```text
capability-executor-contract-v1
```

That branch should use `runtime/router/` as the canonical router contract import path and remain descriptor/contract-only.
